rs.githubusercontent.com/u/51231103?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994","html_url":"https://github.com/JoeyT1994","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JoeyT1994/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"parents":[{"sha":"4e048ec8a2888f198f5432efd7f201f98d473878","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/commits/4e048ec8a2888f198f5432efd7f201f98d473878","html_url":"https://github.com/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/commit/4e048ec8a2888f198f5432efd7f201f98d473878"}]}],"files":[{"sha":"2547d03817f31ee034e85246d0bfc33bc45b1a7a","filename":"proof/atlas/results/RECEIPT.md","status":"modified","additions":3,"deletions":2,"changes":5,"blob_url":"https://github.com/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/blob/3a79a98fb3792ba9f4470a209123ac90c4ba23d1/proof%2Fatlas%2Fresults%2FRECEIPT.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/raw/3a79a98fb3792ba9f4470a209123ac90c4ba23d1/proof%2Fatlas%2Fresults%2FRECEIPT.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/contents/proof%2Fatlas%2Fresults%2FRECEIPT.md?ref=3a79a98fb3792ba9f4470a209123ac90c4ba23d1","patch":"@@ -11,7 +11,8 @@\n | `certify.py` | 37 chunks: **12,021 certified, 0 failures** (`receipts/step4_certify_*.txt`) |\n | `nonempty.py` | F6 is in the interior of Record 877: ‖h(A·F6 − P_t)‖ ≤ 0.0232 < 0.08 (Arb) |\n | `anchor.py` | H₀ (`lean/NoFourMUBs/Step2/BaseAnchor.lean`) is in the interior of Record 9319: ‖h(A·H₀ − P_t)‖ ≤ 0.0426 < 0.08 (Arb) |\n-| Independent checker | `../../independent/results_v3/RESULT.txt`: **12,021 / 12,021 closed Records PASS**, F6 nonemptiness CERTIFIED (Record 877, ≤ 0.02320 < 0.08), all targets closed. VERDICT: the certificate is complete and every check passed |\n+| Independent checker, fresh full run | `../../independent/results_v3_fresh/`: rusty job 7213978 (128 threads, 8 h, 11 Oct), every record recomputed from scratch: **12,021 / 12,021 PASS**, F6 CERTIFIED, complete; sanity tests pass. Row for row identical (timings aside) to the incremental run below |\n+| Independent checker, incremental | `../../independent/results_v3/RESULT.txt`: **12,021 / 12,021 closed Records PASS**, F6 nonemptiness CERTIFIED (Record 877, ≤ 0.02320 < 0.08), all targets closed. VERDICT: the certificate is complete and every check passed |\n \n ## What changed from v2, and why\n \n@@ -24,7 +25,7 @@ This is a failure to certify, not a counterexample. The two implementations clus\n 2. **Reopen.** It reopened the 18 Records whose boundary trees used 11403.\n 3. **Re-close.** `atlas.py` re-closed them (`atlas_run5.log`), spawning one new Record (12020).\n \n-The independent run on v3 reused v2 rows only where the inputs are byte-identical. A Step 3 row was reused when the Record's phases, radius, label radius and frame were unchanged. A Step 4 row was reused only when, in addition, the Record's target list and all its targets were unchanged. It recomputed 2 Step 3 rows (11403, 12020) and 19 Step 4 rows. The checker is deterministic, so a reused row is exactly what a fresh run would produce.\n+The independent run on v3 reused v2 rows only where the inputs are byte-identical. A Step 3 row was reused when the Record's phases, radius, label radius and frame were unchanged. A Step 4 row was reused only when, in addition, the Record's target list and all its targets were unchanged. It recomputed 2 Step 3 rows (11403, 12020) and 19 Step 4 rows. The checker is deterministic, so a reused row is exactly what a fresh run would produce; the fresh full run on rusty (`results_v3_fresh/`) confirms this row for row.\n \n **What a PASS establishes**, together with `PROOF.md`: every Record excludes quartet edges throughout its ball (Lemmas 3.1 and 3.2); every boundary Hadamard of every Record has an interior representative in some Record, up to equivalence, conjugation and transposition (Lemma 4.1); F6 lies in the union; and so does the matched maximum anchor H₀ (needed by the Lean route `no_four_mubs_main`).\n "},{"sha":"f4c179ae6f3ce3bd194c491d9d3f74497b512826","filename":"proof/independent/README.md","status":"modified","additions":7,"deletions":0,"changes":7,"blob_url":"https://github.com/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/blob/3a79a98fb3792ba9f4470a209123ac90c4ba23d1/proof%2Findependent%2FREADME.md","raw_url":"https://github.com/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/raw/3a79a98fb3792ba9f4470a209123ac90c4ba23d1/proof%2Findependent%2FREADME.md","contents_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/JoeyT1994/NoFourMUBS/contents/proof%2Findependent%2FREADME.md?ref=3a79a98fb3792ba9f4470a209123ac90c4ba23d1","patch":"@@ -271,3 +271,10 @@ has to resolve.\n 10. **The export format and \"closed\".** In the test certificate every closed record's targets include non-closed\n     records. A complete certificate must have every target closed. The checker reports this separately\n     (\"All targets closed\").\n+\n+## Runs on the v3 certificate (11 Oct 2026)\n+\n+- `results_v3_fresh/`: fresh, complete run on rusty (`run_rusty.sh`, job 7213978, one 128-core node, 8 h): 12,021 / 12,021 closed Records PASS, F6 nonemptiness CERTIFIED, sanity checks pass.\n+- `results_v3/`: an earlier incremental run reusing byte-identical v2 rows; identical to the fresh run row for row.\n+- The F6 search is now multithreaded over candidate Records (`src/boundary.jl`); only the search is parallel, and each acceptance is the same interval test.\n+"},{"sha":"2aefd5611c00d332432f6a8b